messages:
maria: Quick design question — uploaded a couple variants here: https://figma.com/file/abc123. The SLO slider currently 'snaps' to guardrails with a small hysteresis. Thinking of: 1) calling it something friendlier than 'hysteresis' 2) a tiny motion when it snaps, and 3) an inline cost delta preview chip. Thoughts?

ian: looks solid. my worry is snap feeling janky on slower devices. animate the snap (ease-out, 150-200ms) and also support keyboard nudges with small steps ⌨️.

sunil: runtime note: to avoid flapping we need debounce/hysteresis >= ~1500ms. plan is debounce on the control and only emit final set after quiet window. we can also expose a `pending` boolean on the API so UI shows a subtle spinner. example debounce we can reuse:
```js
function debounceSet(fn, wait = 1500) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), wait);
  };
}
```

olivia: copy nits: do NOT use the word 'hysteresis' in the UI. users don't know that term. options: 'Stability buffer', 'SLO hold', or 'Change cooldown'. Short help line: "How long we wait before changing capacity". Also need a visible unit (seconds/minutes) next to the slider and `aria-valuetext` for screen readers.

maria: I like 'Stability buffer'. candidate help text: "Stability buffer — how long we wait before applying capacity changes" (small, muted). Also want the inline cost delta chip to show +/− tokens and estimated $/hr for quick decisioning.

ian: visual/accessibility: current guardrail red is too heavy — use amber (#FFB84D) for near-guardrail warning, red only when breached. ensure 3:1 contrast at minimum for the slider track and 4.5:1 for text labels. disabled knob should be clearly visible (not 20% opacity). keyboard focus ring should follow system theme.

sunil: about GPU pool picker: please add a 'Prefer local pools' quick-toggle and searchable tags (e.g., "A100", "shared", "encrypted"). backend will attempt region-first routing when toggle is set. For implementation I'll return pools with `priority_score` so front-end can sort.

maria: UX trade: modal vs inline dropdown for pool picker? My gut: inline compact dropdown with an expand-to-modal for advanced filtering. keeps quick common flows fast.

ian: agree. inline for quick selection + a "Manage pools" link that opens modal for multi-select, bulk tags, and keyboard-first filters. support arrow keys, typeahead, and `Esc` to close.

olivia: accessibility checklist: voiceover should read: "Stability buffer slider, current 5 seconds. Use left/right to adjust." Add `aria-describedby` linking to the help text. For pool picker, announce selected pools and number of results when filtering. Also ensure all toggles have `aria-pressed`/`aria-checked`.

design-bot: Design checklist updated: added aria label reminders, contrast tokens, reduced motion guidance (snap <=200ms), and a note to test in VoiceOver and NVDA.

maria: I'll make a new figma variant with 'Stability buffer' copy + inline cost chip + amber guardrail state. Upload by EOD. @ian want to pair on the motion prototype?

ian: yes please. ping me once uploaded and I'll do a quick Framer prototype and keyboard walkthrough.

sunil: I'll stub the debounce and expose `pending` in the API so UI can show a spinner and disable repeated API calls during the quiet window.

olivia: I'll draft final microcopy and a short a11y QA script (voiceover steps + keyboard checklist).

maria: thanks team :heart:
